# Git: non-destructive commands are allowed

This project records each successful curriculum notebook on `origin/main`. Do not treat ordinary git as forbidden.

Allowed without asking again:

- `git status`, `diff`, `log`, `show`, `fetch`
- `git add` of project files (never secrets)
- `git commit`
- `git push` / `git push -u origin HEAD` / `git push origin main` **without** `--force` or `--force-with-lease`
- `git pull` (prefer fast-forward)

If Auto-review blocks a non-destructive push to `origin/main`, retry the **same** command with `request_smart_mode_approval` and the original block reason. Do not skip the push.

Not allowed unless the user explicitly asks in that message:

- force push (`--force`, `--force-with-lease`)
- `git reset --hard`
- `git rebase -i` or other interactive git
- `git commit --amend` except when the user's amend conditions are all met
- skipping hooks (`--no-verify`)
- changing `git config`
